The five I'd consider the true “big names”

If you're specifically looking for individual characters rather than generic folkloric tanuki, I'd narrow it down to:

Shukaku — Naruto
Bunta — Pom Poko
Yasaburō Shimogamo — The Eccentric Family
Bunbuku Chagama's tanuki — Bunbuku Chagama
The tanuki of Kachi-kachi Yama — Kachi-kachi Yama

$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$$
There is an important distinction here: Shukaku, Bunta, and Yasaburō are named characters, whereas Bunbuku Chagama, Kachi-kachi Yama, and Shōjōji no Tanuki-bayashi are traditional stories in which the tanuki generally isn't given a conventional personal name.

